\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Information-level audits on published data (threshold $\tau = 0$). Identified sets are reported per level; at L3 the set is a point (crude risk difference) and the bracketed interval is the 95\%~CI, which is sampling uncertainty, not an identification bound. L1/L2 are deliberate ablations where L3 was published (RECOVERY); for ISIS-2 patient strata, L2/L3 are genuinely unreachable because only odds reductions were published.}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:levels}{{2}{7}{Information-level audits on published data (threshold $\tau = 0$). Identified sets are reported per level; at L3 the set is a point (crude risk difference) and the bracketed interval is the 95\%~CI, which is sampling uncertainty, not an identification bound. L1/L2 are deliberate ablations where L3 was published (RECOVERY); for ISIS-2 patient strata, L2/L3 are genuinely unreachable because only odds reductions were published}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Identified sets by information level. Grey: L1 (arm totals only); blue: L2 (plus stratum denominators, LP bounds); red point and whiskers: L3 (plus arm-by-stratum counts; point with 95\%~CI). For ISIS-2 patient strata only L1 is reachable. For RECOVERY, L1/L2 are ablations of genuinely published L3 tables.}}{7}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:levels}{{1}{7}{Identified sets by information level. Grey: L1 (arm totals only); blue: L2 (plus stratum denominators, LP bounds); red point and whiskers: L3 (plus arm-by-stratum counts; point with 95\%~CI). For ISIS-2 patient strata only L1 is reachable. For RECOVERY, L1/L2 are ablations of genuinely published L3 tables}{figure.1}{}}
